From 2d09e0a48567a551c853ee7ee44936da777f4890 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:42:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip(host-read-transport): adaptive transport -- optimistic
 map start, stall detection + probe-fill A/B, and `--load-mode buffered`

Maintainer decisions (2026-11-11) folded in:

  * START OPTIMISTICALLY on the mapping.  No capacity prior selects the arm any more: the mapping is
    the fastest arm whenever the page cache holds the set (17 GiB/s random warm vs 7 for a buffered
    read) and being wrong costs one probe cadence.  The cgroup-aware `pool_available_ram_bytes()`
    stays as the root-cause fix for the pool RAM ceiling (TODO #306 option 3).
  * NO HARD-CODED MiB/s (or ms) ANYWHERE.  The absolute floor and the epoch-rate collapse test are
    gone -- both were box-specific guesses, and the rate test fired wrongly on a RAM-rich box (measured:
    16 444 -> 9 624 MiB/s for one epoch, which switched a box off the mapping it wants).  Two relative
    triggers remain:
      - STALL: a read over TR_STALL_K x this arm's own running mean, TR_STALL_N times running;
      - PROBE-FILL A/B: every TR_PROBE_FILLS fills, the NEXT arm serves that fill instead.  Same bytes
        (text is byte-identical on every arm), so it costs no extra I/O -- it IS a fill that had to
        happen -- and it is an exact A/B: two latencies, same box, same cache state, same moment.
        TR_PROBE_N consecutive wins by TR_PROBE_GAIN latch the next step.
  * ONE WAY IS THE DECISION: a box that fell short once is likely to again, and the page cache a reverse
    switch would rebuild may itself cause the shortfall, so a slower consistent point beats a flapping
    optimum.  A reverse direction is a later opt-in, not a gap.
  * `--load-mode buffered` (new): a MAPPED master whose host reads are buffered `pread`s -- the
    combination that used to be unrepresentable (r212 welded the fill transport to `--load-mode`, so
    only `dio` ever got a non-mapping read).  Explicit `mmap` / `buffered` / `dio` LOCK the transport;
    `auto` (the default) is the adaptive one.  `none` / `mlock` / `mmap+mlock` keep today's meaning.

Measured on this box (llama-cli, greedy, no -lv unless noted):
  * text identical in all arms: 144 chars sha=de81b28cab7d for mmap / buffered / auto, and for the
    static four-way instrument.
  * `--load-mode buffered` -> `host read transport -> file (pinned by --load-mode)`; `mmap` -> `map`;
    `auto` -> `map (optimistic start)`.
  * `--load-mode dio` builds no pool ("NOT APPLIED: a pool needs a mapped load"), unchanged.
  * auto inside a 32G scope latches on evidence:
    `map -> file (probe fill: file served the same read in 33 us against this arm's 50 us, 3 samples
    running)`.

Owed: the gate (a transition arm + the pinned arms + the span coupling), the interleaved A/B for the
probe knobs, the decode ladder, and a Windows-form measurement.
